hey everyone and welcome to my tutorial  on how to make an origami dragon in  order to make the dragon we first need  to make the bird base which is something  that I go over in my crane tutorial that  you can find in my origami playlist on  my channel I will go over how to make  the bird base in this video also however  I do recommend that you check out my  crane tutorial if you'd like to learn  how to make the Japanese crane what  you're going to need for this tutorial  is a plain sheet of printer paper and  scissors are going to be optional once  you have those items you're ready to  begin so we first need to have a piece  of square paper so what you do with  printer paper is you take the corner and  you line this edge up with this edge by  folding this corner down here then you  make a crease and you cut off the excess  paper okay so now we need to fold the  paper in half by taking the top edge and  aligning it with the bottom edge make a  crease open the paper and then we're  going to fold it in half going the other  way again take the top edge bring it  down to the bottom edge make sure it's  lined up good and then you make another  crease so now you should have a piece of  paper with a cross in it and a diagonal  line so take the paper and fold it on  the diagonal line and just make sure  that it's flat put the paper down on a  hard surface or a table top and what you  want to do now is you want to lift up  the first layer and we're going to tuck  this corner down where my thumb is and  it should go on those folds which you  just made then you can flatten it out do  the same for the other side so lift up  this first layer tuck the corner in like  that and just flatten everything out on  the folds that you made previously  what we're going to do next is to work  on what's known as the petal fold which  is the final fold that we're going to do  in order to get the bird base so to make  things a little bit easier to see on  camera I've drawn a vertical line from  one end here to the other bottom end so  what we want to do next is we want to  take one of these layers and we want to  line up this edge here onto that line  and then we crease so you should have  something that looks like that then you  want to do the same thing with the  remaining three flaps now that we have  something that looks like a kite what we  want to do is to take the top of the  kite and we want to fold the corner down  onto the top of these folds here so if  you picture this as a line you want to  fold the corner directly on that line  just like that and then we're just going  to fold it the other way also alright  what that does is it just helps you do  the petal fold make it a little bit  easier so put the model again on a hard  flat surface open these flaps which we  previously fold it in and then what  we're going to do we're going to lift  this top sheet this top corner and we're  going to pull it upwards and what we  want to do is we want to push it outward  so that these ends these corners here  start to go towards the center of the  model and you might have to push a  little on these folds which we  previously made  so you should have something like that  and what you want to do is just make  sure that the structure is completely  flat flip it over and do the same and  there you go you have the bird base okay  so now that you have your bird base you  want to take these two top points and  you want to hold one in each hand and  you want to pull on them until the top  of that structure goes flat so now  you'll see that the top of it is flat  and then what you do is just flip it  over and put it down like that now what  we're going to do is we're going to just  flatten these two triangle structures  that are sticking up so what you do is  you just take your thumbs and you kind  of push in on the middle of this like  this and you want to just squash it  completely flat just like that turn it  around and do the same thing for this  side so just push in on it like that  and then just press down and then what  you want to do so you should have  something like this then what you want  to do is you want to just take these two  and just flatten them to the right side  and push down make sure everything is  flat and you should have something that  looks like this okay so you want to hold  the model like this with these two arms  facing downward this way then what you  do is you flip the model over completely  now as you'll see I drew another line  that indicates where the center of the  model is what you want to do is you want  to take this edge here and you want to  align it on this line that I have drawn  and then you make a crease do the same  for the other side so now you should  have something that looks like this now  what you want to do is you want to push  down on the middle of this and you want  to fold it in half completely so take  the model now and you should see there  is kind of a fold going this way if you  crease it down you should see it what  you want to do is you just want to make  a fold on that line so just crease it  pretty good turn it around and do the  same for this side okay now what we want  to do is we want to open the middle of  this and we want to lift this piece up  into the middle so it's like this you  want to lift this piece and it should go  on that fold and then all you have to do  is just flatten it out just like that  okay so this is going to be the head of  the dragon and this is going to be the  tail what we want to do is we want to  open this front part and we want to take  these edges here and we want to fold  them down onto the middle line  just like that and do the same for the  left side once you have done that you  want to just close it back up by putting  these ends back together and then you  want to make sure everything is flat  draw a line like this on the neck part  of your model right about there and what  you're going to do is we're just going  to fold on that line something just like  that then you can lift it back up and we  open it we want to just push this part  down on that fold that we just made and  then you want to close the top of it by  just pinching it and you want to make  sure everything is flat then what you  want to do is you want to just open this  top part and you want to fold right  about here so you want to fold it like  that and then you want to just pinch the  top of it again and closed and then you  can lift up this horn here if you want  so now we have formed the head to do the  neck what we do is we just fold the head  down like that and then we can open it  up and we're just going to kind of  squeeze it down there like that now what  you want to do is you want to take these  arms and you want to fold them straight  down so that this is vertical do the  same for the other side okay so to do  the tail if you look at the model you  should see a vertical line that is on  the body of the dragon what you want to  do is you want to take this bottom edge  of the tail and you want to fold it on  that line that's right about there  take it and you fold it up just like  that then what you want to do with the  top is you want to just fold it so that  this part is horizontal right about  halfway just like that  so at 90 degree angles we fold this  directly up and we fold this to the  right at 90 degree angles then you can  just unfold it and what we're going to  do is just open the tail and we're going  to push it up like that just like we did  for the head on that fold and then you  just flatten everything out now that we  have the other fold there what we do is  we just open the center of this again  push down on that fold  so you sit up something like that and  then you could fold it just once more  directly upwards do the same thing you  don't have to be too neat about it  something like that then all we have to  do is to fold the arms by taking it and  folding it towards the center of the  body upwards that way and you want to  fold it just like that so that this edge  actually is on the bottom of the body  right about there  do the same thing for the other side  fold it up and this bottom edge here  should be on the bottom of the body here  just like that and then you just fold it  down and then you can just fold these  straight down like that at 90 degree  angles  and what you do is you just pull on the  arms a little bit and you can open the  tail and there you go you have an  origami dragon

